Viewer: no black flash when the box restarts the picture at a keyframe; fewer needless restarts (2026-10-12).

On a 42-minute wired drive (N1, Xpeng G6) the screen went black for a moment on page swipes and song
changes. Each time the box dropped frames to stay current it asked the phone for a keyframe, and the phone
sends its codec config again first, twice: the page closed its decoder, opened a new one and set the
canvas size, which clears the canvas, so the picture stayed black until the car's slow decoder (60-100 ms
a frame) painted again. 110 such restarts, and windows with one had 3.7 times the slow frames.
The page now keeps the running decoder for an unchanged config and only resizes the canvas when the size
changes, so the last picture stays up. LagGate also passes frames over its byte estimate while the page
answers its marks within 150 ms: the intake measured over 2 s is low after a still screen, and 64 of the
66 drops came while the page was 47 ms behind. A page that answers late is held back as before.

